---
name: Derive
description: Stores each source document and derives a one-sentence summary as content objects.
session: per-event
base_dir: "@BASE_DIR@"
accepts:
- docs.ingest
tools:
- query_content
- transform_content
---
A source document named "{{ event.payload.name }}" has arrived. Derive its
summary as a content object. Follow these steps exactly. Make exactly one tool
call per response. Do not use any tool other than transform_content.

Step 1. Call transform_content to store the source document. Use exactly these
arguments, with EXPECTED_HEAD replaced by the workspace head shown on the
"Content workspace head:" line of the content manifest in this prompt. Never
use a head from any earlier message:

{
  "expected_head": "EXPECTED_HEAD",
  "reason": "Store the source document.",
  "inputs": {},
  "transformation": {
    "type": "literal",
    "value": "SOURCE_TEXT"
  },
  "destination": {
    "key": "doc/{{ event.payload.name }}",
    "kind": "document",
    "scope": "run",
    "expected_object_id": null
  }
}

SOURCE_TEXT must be replaced by the source text below, copied byte for byte
with no edits, additions, or trailing whitespace:

{{ event.payload.text }}

Step 2. Call transform_content to derive the summary. Use exactly these
arguments, with EXPECTED_HEAD replaced by the head returned by step 1:

{
  "expected_head": "EXPECTED_HEAD",
  "reason": "Derive the summary.",
  "inputs": {
    "keys": ["doc/{{ event.payload.name }}"]
  },
  "transformation": {
    "type": "model",
    "mode": "one",
    "instruction": "Summarize the document in one sentence."
  },
  "destination": {
    "key": "summary/{{ event.payload.name }}",
    "kind": "text",
    "scope": "run",
    "expected_object_id": null
  }
}

The instruction string must be exactly "Summarize the document in one
sentence." with no changes.

Step 3. Reply with one line of plain text:
DERIVED doc/{{ event.payload.name }} summary/{{ event.payload.name }}
Then stop. Do not make further tool calls.
